Saphira OpenStack controller role
===================================

Install this package on the machine that will run the control plane:
keystone, glance, placement, the nova API/conductor/scheduler,
the neutron API + RPC server, horizon, and the supporting
infrastructure (mariadb, rabbitmq, memcached).

Then run, as root:

    saphira-openstack-setup-controller

Answer five questions. The script writes every configuration file,
bootstraps the databases, registers all endpoints, starts every
service, and proves each one answers. Re-running is safe.

Verify later with:

    saphira-openstack-setup-controller --check

What the script deliberately does NOT do: it never touches compute
or storage nodes (sibling packages), never enables anything at
install time, and never stores your passwords.

Full story (how-to, pitfalls, do and don't):
saphira-openstack-documentation.
Saphira Linux — "It's so Simple it Hurts."
